WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.230
The Game of Thrones epic prequel series, House
of the Dragon, is coming, and many epic characters

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.260
with it as well, from Targaryens to many other
houses and many other legendary figures from

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.250
that time period as well.
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.640
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president
to air in 2022.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:23.529
Filming begins with the start of 2021.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:28.730
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:31.390
producer.
It’s based on George RR Martin’s book

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.230
Fire And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s
yet unfinished Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.710
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:45.330
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:50.460
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:54.800
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.
The yet unreleased Fire And Vlood volume 2

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.720
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:05.909
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:01:05.909 --> 00:01:10.490
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
The key event of the show is also the key

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:15.259
in the history of House Targaryen, the Dance
of the Dragons - the Targaryen civil war,

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:20.659
which divided the entire kingdom and launched
a huge war that was fought from 129 AC to

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:26.439
131 AC. When King Viserys died, his oldest
child, Rhaenyra, was expected to ascend the

00:01:26.439 --> 00:01:32.180
Iron Throne, since her father did not change
the succession when he had a son Aegon. However,

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:38.079
Aegon II Targaryen was crowned King in the
Dragonpit, at bequest of Alicent Hightower.

00:01:38.079 --> 00:01:41.820
The war between brother and sister would be
known as the Dance of the Dragons.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.939
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:51.290
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:54.279
I's throne.
Both of them thought they belonged on the

00:01:54.279 --> 00:01:58.650
Iron Throne. When people started declaring
for one of them or the other, their fight

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:03.350
divided the kingdoms in two.
Targaryens fought Targaryens, brothers fought

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:08.150
brothers, dragons fought dragons. By the time
it was over, thousands were dead.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:12.480
The conflict would prove to be incredibly
destructive for not only House Targaryen,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:18.050
but large parts of Westeros as well. In addition,
it devastated the Targaryen's dragon population,

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:21.290
ultimately leading to their extinction within
a few decades.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:26.201
By the end of the reign of King Viserys I
Targaryen, twenty dragons were alive. The

00:02:26.201 --> 00:02:30.580
majority of these died during the civil war
called the Dance of the Dragons, which began

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:37.420
in 129 AC and lasted until mid 131 AC.
One of the main characters from this time

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.380
period was Rhaenys Targaryen, Rhaenyra's right
hand.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:46.341
Princess Rhaenys Targaryen, known among the
smallfolk as the Queen Who Never Was, was

00:02:46.341 --> 00:02:53.240
the daughter of Prince Aemon Targaryen and
Lady Jocelyn Baratheon born in 74 AC on the

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:57.630
seventh day of the seventh month. Rhaenys
Targaryen was the granddaughter of Jaehaerys

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:04.340
I Targaryen, and the cousin of Viserys I Targaryen
and Daemon Targaryen. Rhaenys was a great

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:07.030
beauty.
She was a clever, capable, spirited, proud,

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:10.500
fierce, and fearless woman. She had a fiery
temperament.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:16.030
Rhaenys wore steel and copper armor which
flashed on the sun. As her father was the

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:21.520
Prince of Dragonstone, and she was his firstborn
child, many considered her as being next in

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:27.120
line for the Iron Throne, after her father
Aemon. Queen Alysanne Targaryen, when being

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.300
presented with her granddaughter, called her
"our queen to be". Rhaenys became a dragonrider

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:38.740
in 87 AC when she claimed the dragon Meleys,
the Red Queen. Rhaenys married legendary Corlys

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:44.390
of House Velaryion, known as the Sea Snake,
in 90 AC at the age of sixteen. Rhaenys's

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:48.220
father, Prince Aemon Targaryen, died in 92
AC.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:53.230
As Aemon had been the Prince of Dragonstone,
King Jaehaerys I Targaryen had to formally

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.520
appoint a new heir to the Iron Throne. The
choice was between Rhaenys, Aemon's only child

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:05.210
and heir, and Aemon's brother Baelon. Jaehaerys
appointed Baelon as the new Prince of Dragonstone,

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:10.640
passing over the pregnant Rhaenys and her
unborn child. Rhaenys herself was the first

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.970
to object to the king's decision, and her
husband, Lord Corlys Velaryon, gave up his

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:19.769
position as lord admiral and his place on
the small council. Following that, Rhaenys

00:04:19.769 --> 00:04:25.760
and her husband returned to Driftmark. Others
angered by the king's decision included Rhaenys's

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:31.540
mother, Lady Jocelyn Baratheon, her uncle,
Lord Boremund Baratheon, and her grandmother,

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:37.720
King Jaehaerys's wife, Queen Alysanne Targaryen.
Rhaenys gave birth to her first child, a daughter

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:42.190
she named Laena Velaryon, late in the year
92 AC.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:47.490
The following year, she gave birth to a son,
Laenor Velaryon. Although both House Velaryon

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:52.210
and House Baratheon insisted that Laenor had
the better claim to the throne, Prince Baelon

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:57.281
remained King Jaehaerys's heir.
When Baelon died in 101 AC, King Jaehaerys

00:04:57.281 --> 00:05:02.960
called the first Great Council at Harrenhal
to decide the matter of succession. Fourteen

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:08.210
claims were considered, including the claims
of Rhaenys and her children. Rhaenys's uncle,

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:12.830
Lord Boremund Baratheon, was outspoken in
supporting the claims of Rhaenys and her son

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:18.350
Laenor during the Great Council, and Lord
Ellard Stark gave his support to Rhaenys and

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:23.360
Corlys as well. Other supporters included
House Dustin of Barrowton and House Manderly

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:28.040
of White Harbor. Yet the claims of Rhaenys
and her daughter were rejected on account

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:32.920
that they are females. Rhaenys and Corlys
used their wealth and influence to persuade

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:38.370
the lords present to vote for their son Laenor,
one of the two primary claimants. For this,

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:43.930
they received support from Lord Boremund,
Lord Ellard, Lord Manderly, Lord Dustin, Lord

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:49.360
Blackwood, Lord Bar Emmon, Lord Celtigar,
as well as others. However, Laenor was eventually

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:55.530
passed over in favor of Baelon's son Viserys.
While the vote was kept secret, it was rumored

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:58.919
the assembled lords favored Viserys by twenty
to one.

00:05:58.919 --> 00:06:02.490
For having been passed over in the line of
succession once again,

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:06.490
the court jester Mushroom would name her "The
Queen Who Never Was".

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:11.570
Following the death of Queen Aemma Arryn,
in 105 AC, Grand Maester Runciter suggested

00:06:11.570 --> 00:06:16.730
to King Viserys I Targaryen that he shall
take Rhaenys's twelve-year-old daughter, Laena,

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:21.310
to wife.
King Viserys, however, chose Alicent Hightower.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:25.919
Angered by the third time she and her family
had been scorned by House Targaryen, Rhaenys

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:29.860
and her family did not attend the royal wedding
in 106 AC.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:35.530
In 113 AC, King Viserys I and his small council
began discussions concerning a betrothal for

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:42.430
Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen, Viserys's heir.
They eventually agreed on Rhaenys's son, Laenor.

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:47.870
Rhaenyra and Laenor were wed the next year.
Rhaenys's daughter Laena was married to Daemon

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:54.760
Targaryen, the Rogue Prince. Both of Rhaenys's
children died in 120 AC; Laena died in childbirth

00:06:54.760 --> 00:07:00.389
during the early days of the year, while Laenor
was killed by Ser Qarl Correy while attending

00:07:00.389 --> 00:07:04.680
a fair in Spicetown.
When the Dance of the Dragons began in 129

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:09.930
AC, Princess Rhaenys sat on the black council
of Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen, the daughter

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:15.470
of the late King Viserys I Targaryen. When
the Velaryon fleet closed off the Gullet,

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:20.360
sailing forth from Dragonstone and Driftmark
to block all shipping for Blackwater Bay,

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:24.699
the blacks' plan was for Rhaenys to fly overhead
on Meleys to keep the greens from attacking

00:07:24.699 --> 00:07:29.090
their ships with dragons. When news arrived
on Dragonstone about the death of Lucerys

00:07:29.090 --> 00:07:34.740
Velaryon at the hands of Prince Aemond Targaryen,
Rhaenys and her husband prevented Lucerys's

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:39.930
brother Joffrey from mounting his dragon to
avenge his brother. Grief-stricken following

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:45.780
the death of Lucerys, Queen Rhaenyra Targaryen
gave Rhaenys and Corlys command over her war

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:50.630
council. When Rook's Rest was attacked by
Ser Criston Cole and the Greens, as Aegon

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:56.169
II's supporters were called, Rhaenyra sent
her aunt to burn the army and save the fort.

00:07:56.169 --> 00:08:02.390
Mounted on her dragon, Meleys, Rhaenys unexpectedly
turned up at Rook's Rest and laid waste to

00:08:02.390 --> 00:08:05.949
the enemy army. However, Rhaenys was flying
into a trap.

00:08:05.949 --> 00:08:12.090
Her nephew Aemond Targaryen confronted her
on his monstrous dragon Vhagar, the last of

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:17.900
the original three Targaryen dragons that
conquered Westeros, along with the King himself,

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:23.729
on his magnificent dragon Sunfyre. Despite
being outnumbered, Rhaenys did not flee.

00:08:23.729 --> 00:08:28.070
Rhaenys turned to meet the attack, despite
the knowledge that Meleys stood no chance

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:34.099
against the two dragons. Meleys's flame faced
Vhagar's and Sunfyre's, until it looked like

00:08:34.099 --> 00:08:38.350
that there was a second sun in the sky. The
three dragons attacked each other and fell

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:42.729
to the ground, entangled.
By the time the fight was over, Aemond and

00:08:42.729 --> 00:08:46.940
Vhagar were the only ones uninjured,
while Aegon had to have a constant dose of

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:51.260
milk of the poppy to survive
and Sunfyre (who laid on top of Aegon) was

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:56.580
wounded, and a wing almost completely torn
off. It was crippled and would never fly again.

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:00.790
Meleys had been "torn to shreds" and Rhaenys
was just ash and bone.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:05.510
That was Rhaenys's brave last stand where
she died for Rhaenyra's cause.

00:09:05.510 --> 00:09:11.060
Rhaenys's husband Corlys, the Sea Snake, was
enraged that Rhaenyra had sent his wife Rhaenys

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:17.020
to the battle alone rather than going herself
or ordering her sons to accompany Rhaenys.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:21.830
"Beloved daughter of Lady Jocelyn Baratheon
and Prince Aemon Targaryen, faithful wife

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:27.230
of Lord Corlys Velaryon, mother and grandmother,
the Queen Who Never Was lived fearlessly,

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:32.730
and died amidst blood and fire. She was fifty-five
years old." - is how Gyldayn describes her

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:36.160
in Fire And Blood.
Rhaenys Targaryen will definitely be one of

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:40.980
my favorite characters in the House of the
Dragon, fierce and smart woman, brave and

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:45.880
loyal. Honorable woman who upholds her oath
to Queen Rhaenyra and who fought for her cause

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:51.540
so forcefully that not even Vhagar and Sunfyre
combined could fear her away.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:56.000
Legendary characters such as Rhaenys Targaryen,
legendary battles such as the siege of Rook's

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:01.360
Rest in which Rhaenys flew her dragon, the
Red Queen, straight into Aegon and Aemond

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:06.650
despite being outnumbered by their two dragons
out of which one was mighty Vhagar. Rhaenys

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:11.710
could have fled, but she chose to fight and
went down in epic battle, in fire and blood.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:15.160
All of that and more this Game of Thrones
prequel show, House of the Dragon, brings

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:18.300
in 2022.
Thank you so much for watching, hope you enjoyed

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.854
this video, and if you did make sure to give
it a big thumbs up and I hope to see you in

00:10:20.854 --> 00:10:27.410
the next one, peace!

